    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493296733/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Saturday February 22 /02.  I Tatti
The Houghtons and Mr. Rosenheim to lunch. Bach concert afterwards. Horne to dine. 
Sunday February 23. 1902
Had a delightful drive to La Quiete, then a walk through the Careggi woods. B.B. then called on Horne and Logan and I on Donna Lucrezia Corsini – nice, fresh, hearty creature.
Monday  February 24. 1902.
Music lesson – Concert. Bernhard in Uffizi. I finished  Clarissa Harlowe , nine volumes of what comes perilously close to twaddle, but somehow manages to be interesting.  Don Quixote  is enchanting!"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 229 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1899-02> .

